    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-09T09:18:01+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-09T09:18:01+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-08T23:48:01Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-08T23:48:01Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred south of WA extends a ridge across the south of SA. The main high centre will move eastwards during the week to be centred to the east of SA on Friday. A trough over the interior of WA will remain stationary for most of the week and may extend into the far west of SA at times. Another low pressure trough will approach from the west on Saturday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW010" description="West Coast" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-09T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-10T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-08T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-09T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Medium chance of showers west of Nullarbor, becoming less likely in the late afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Winds southeasterly 25 to 40 km/h decreasing to 20 to 30 km/h in the evening. Daytime maximum temperatures around 18.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:40am to 3:20pm, UV Index predicted to reach 6 [High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-10T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-11T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-09T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-10T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower west of Nullarbor, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Nullarbor in the early morning. Winds southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h turning easterly early in the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 4 and 7 with daytime temperatures reaching around 20.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-11T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-12T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-10T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-11T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers west of Nullarbor in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Nullarbor in the morning. Winds easterly 15 to 20 km/h turning northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 9 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-12T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-13T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-11T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-12T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers west of Nullarbor in the evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Ceduna in the evening. Winds northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h turning northerly during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to around 10 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
